WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:06.920
Hi I'm Julie Stanford and my superpower is&nbsp;
designing technologies and experiences that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:13.160
love. I wear two hats. Half my time I'm at the&nbsp;
Stanford computer science department where I teach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.560
learners like you how to do research and design&nbsp;
for technological change. The other half of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.480
time, I'm at Slice Bread a consulting agency I&nbsp;
founded where I practice what I preach. Through my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:30.520
consulting work I've witnessed many well-intended&nbsp;
digital transformation projects with with low&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:36.480
adoption, lots of headaches along the way. Here's&nbsp;
what I've learned from these failed projects. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.840
though the term digital transformation sounds&nbsp;
like it's about technology, turns out the secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:49.680
to success is to shift your focus to the people at&nbsp;
the center. If you want to make sure that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:56.400
technologies you introduce have long-term impact,&nbsp;
you need to start with a human-centered approach.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.960
We'll begin this course by taking a deep dive&nbsp;
into interview techniques that you can employ to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:09.600
uncover the true root causes of problems. Then&nbsp;
we'll learn how to squeeze as much insight as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.640
we can from that data. And finally we'll cover a&nbsp;
systematic process for running rapid experiments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:22.840
to validate your ideas and minimize risk at every&nbsp;
step. Along the way we'll analyze case studies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.600
and you'll work through project-based exercises&nbsp;
that will help you apply what you've learned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.800
What are some of the things you do at the&nbsp;
beginning. Business leader Jonathan Alloy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.200
will provide additional industry insights on how&nbsp;
to plan, test, and launch an effective digital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.360
transformation What you really have to do is&nbsp;
step outside of your own preconceived biases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:50.560
and truly listen. Be willing to follow up and&nbsp;
dig and probe and ask why. My goal is to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.520
you up-level your career by teaching you how&nbsp;
to use human centered tools to confidently run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:07.880
a successful digital transformation project. So&nbsp;
join us from wherever you are at Stanford Online.

